<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Nuhashshe</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 BCE – 1300 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Nuhashshe, a group of small Syrian kingdoms between the Orontes and the Euphrates, fought over by Mitanni, Egypt and the Hittites.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The lands of Nuhashshe lay in the steppe and farmland south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>. In the 15th century BCE their rulers were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mitanni-empire">Mitanni Empire</a>, and the region appears in Egyptian records of campaigns by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a> and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarna-letters">Amarna letters</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nuhashshe was a cluster of local kingdoms rather than a single state, with a leading king who represented the region in treaties. Its rulers moved between Egyptian, Mitannian and Hittite loyalties as each power advanced.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suppiluliuma-i">Suppiluliuma I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> conquered the region in the 14th century BCE and made its king a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> by treaty. Rebellions under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mursili-ii">Mursili II</a> were suppressed, and the region later reappeared as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/luash">Lu'ash</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 BCE – 1300 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:29.85%;width:3.98%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 BCE – 1300 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sharrupshi, Tette</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hurrian and Syrian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Akkadian, Hurrian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nuhasse, Lands of Nuhashshe</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1400&amp;focus=nuhashshe" aria-label="Nuhashshe on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5647 924 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Nuhashshe lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5996 1079h0M5852 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5967 1180h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5967 1180h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Syria. <a href="/atlas?year=-1400&amp;focus=nuhashshe">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

